# Roodogs Coach — environment variables
#
# The app works with NONE of these set: it just runs on each device on its own
# (localStorage only). Set the cloud store variables to turn on cross-device
# sync so your computer and phone share one dataset.

# --- Cross-device sync store (Redis REST) ---
# The easiest way to get these is the Vercel Marketplace: your project →
# Storage → add "Upstash for Redis" (free tier). Vercel injects these two
# automatically, so you normally don't paste them by hand.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Alternative names, if you connect Upstash directly rather than via Vercel.
# Only one pair is needed; the app accepts either.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Optional hardening ---
# If set, the sync endpoint requires this exact value as a bearer token.
# The app sends the team password (lib/appConfig.ts), so set this to the SAME
# value as that password, or leave it unset to keep the endpoint open (the
# soft gate that already fronts the app). For a kids' team with first names
# only, unset is fine.
# SYNC_PASSWORD=

# --- Local testing only — never set this in Vercel ---
# Uses an in-process memory store instead of Redis, so two browser windows
# against one `next start` can exercise sync without any cloud account.
# SYNC_DEV_STORE=1
